{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04T3", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-stack-to-presentation}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3a2cf1e8a8de0e6bf529e5b6d1b08cc87ea8383c480385a9d787cc0789241e93", "source_text": "From an algebraic stack to a presentation", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cc9c6832991f1f79f2b75783b079515f94803b256d70e800c5c2f8fb09966a1f", "unit_id": "tag:04T3:title"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04T3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$[U/R]$", "MATH_0006": "$[U/R]$", "MATH_0007": "$[U/R]$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-groupoids-definition-quotient-stack}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "TEXTBFCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTBFOPEN_0001": "{\\bf "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a7f99d1743db24ace72b3a6d80c1ffacd9fd485f16cbb3b5069db6e9b7ee1fb7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:10362b31e5f50597cb690c0b6ab9c494aa17edb6e06c9f5ba630d55da7988531", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nGiven an algebraic stack over <MATH_0001> we obtain a groupoid in algebraic spaces\nover <MATH_0002> whose associated quotient stack is the algebraic stack.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nRecall that if <MATH_0003> is a groupoid in algebraic spaces over <MATH_0004>\nthen <MATH_0005> denotes the quotient stack associated to this datum, see\nGroupoids in Spaces,\nDefinition <REF_0001>.\nIn general <MATH_0006> is <TEXTBFOPEN_0001>not<TEXTBFCLOSE_0001> an algebraic stack. In particular the\nstack <MATH_0007> occurring in the following lemma is in general not\nalgebraic.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:185170edf238dee7adfc43b6dbb72ed8a033b7eef1f4648c8fb6ee92003bab12", "unit_id": "tag:04T3:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04T3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$f : \\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0008": "$2$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{R} = \\mathcal{U} \\times_{f, \\mathcal{X}, f} \\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\mathcal{U} \\times_{f, \\mathcal{X}, f} \\mathcal{U}\n\\times_{f, \\mathcal{X}, f} \\mathcal{U} =\n\\mathcal{R} \\times_{\\text{pr}_1, \\mathcal{U}, \\text{pr}_0} \\mathcal{R},\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$\\text{pr}_{02}$", "MATH_0012": "$1$", "MATH_0013": "$$\n\\text{pr}_{02} :\n\\mathcal{R} \\times_{\\text{pr}_1, \\mathcal{U}, \\text{pr}_0} \\mathcal{R}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{R}\n$$", "MATH_0014": "$U$", "MATH_0015": "$R$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{R}$", "MATH_0017": "$t, s : R \\to U$", "MATH_0018": "$c : R \\times_{s, U, t} R \\to R$", "MATH_0019": "$1$", "MATH_0020": "$\\text{pr}_0, \\text{pr}_1 : \\mathcal{R} \\to \\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0021": "$\\text{pr}_{02} :\n\\mathcal{R} \\times_{\\text{pr}_1, \\mathcal{U}, \\text{pr}_0} \\mathcal{R} \\to\n\\mathcal{R}$", "MATH_0022": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0023": "$S$", "MATH_0024": "$f$", "MATH_0025": "$1$", "MATH_0026": "$f_{can} : [U/R] \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0027": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0028": "$1$", "MATH_0029": "$f_{can} : [U/R] \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-map-space-into-stack}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fd2f4cc4b426f3005a42e70ed99a74dc6c35cb824150a05a4a0fc88e88f33c33", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:03ca5cd24ac6dff18d1346d56640d404bc98ddfed7babf0526c813b72aca93eb", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be an algebraic stack over <MATH_0004>.\nLet <MATH_0005> be an algebraic stack over <MATH_0006> which\nis representable by an algebraic space.\nLet <MATH_0007> be a 1-morphism. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the <MATH_0008>-fibre product\n<MATH_0009>\nis representable by an algebraic space,\n<STRUCT_0003> there is a canonical equivalence\n<MATH_0010>\n<STRUCT_0004> the projection <MATH_0011> induces via (2) a <MATH_0012>-morphism\n<MATH_0013>\n<STRUCT_0005> let <MATH_0014>, <MATH_0015> be the algebraic spaces representing\n<MATH_0016> and <MATH_0017> and\n<MATH_0018> are the morphisms corresponding\nto the <MATH_0019>-morphisms\n<MATH_0020>\nand\n<MATH_0021> above, then the quintuple <MATH_0022> is a groupoid in\nalgebraic spaces over <MATH_0023>,\n<STRUCT_0006> the morphism <MATH_0024> induces a canonical <MATH_0025>-morphism\n<MATH_0026>\nof stacks in groupoids over <MATH_0027>, and\n<STRUCT_0007> the <MATH_0028>-morphism <MATH_0029> is fully faithful.\n<STRUCT_0008>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7d56fd8149e4d83abb9914601f2d08cce45c9c5e2882a31e1090439a0f27bcf1", "unit_id": "tag:04T4:statement"}
